<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<PLUGIN name="unraid-deck-bridge" author="mccray" version="2026.10.29a" min="6.12.0" icon="releases/2026.10.29a-4c0ae45f48af/assets/unraid-deck-bridge.png" pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mccray-s/unraid-deck-bridge/main/unraid-deck-bridge.plg" support="https://github.com/mccray-s/unraid-deck-bridge/issues" project="https://github.com/mccray-s/unraid-deck-bridge"><CHANGES>###2026.10.29a
- Change: Use one date-based release identity across the native plugin, Bridge, Core, diagnostics, and release artifacts.
- Fix: Activate upgrades from legacy Bridge 0.1.1 through the normal native plugin update without removing settings or task journals.
- Fix: Restart the previous runtime safely after a failed same-day revision upgrade.
- Fix: Preserve full native changelog history and reject inconsistent or overwritten release artifacts.

###2026.10.29
- Fix: Wait for stable API startup before activating Bridge.
- Change: Reload the API only when extension registration or the loaded adapter requires it.
- Add: Retain bounded lifecycle diagnostics across reboots.

###2026.10.28
- Initial Release: Native Unraid Deck Bridge plugin with the GraphQL adapter and Core runtime.</CHANGES><FILE Run="/bin/bash"><INLINE>set -euo pipefail
if [ "$(uname -s)" != Linux ] || [ "$(uname -m)" != x86_64 ]; then
  echo 'Bridge requires Linux x86_64 (Unraid)' &gt;&amp;2
  exit 1
fi
[ -f /etc/unraid-version ] || { echo 'Bridge requires Unraid: /etc/unraid-version is missing' &gt;&amp;2; exit 1; }
for dependency in node unraid-api tar sha256sum flock mktemp install curl mv; do
  command -v "$dependency" &gt;/dev/null || { echo "Bridge requires dependency: $dependency" &gt;&amp;2; exit 1; }
done
node -e 'if(process.arch!=="x64")process.exit(1)' || { echo 'Bridge requires Node x64 on Linux x86_64' &gt;&amp;2; exit 1; }
